Package: homelab-agent
Architecture: all
Depends: perl (>= 5.36),
         homelab-common,
         libmojolicious-perl,
         libyaml-libyaml-perl,
         adduser
Description: Per-host fleet agent: declarative service manifest + heartbeat + live status
 Every homelab-* package that has something worth watching (a systemd
 unit, a listening port) drops a small YAML file into
 /etc/homelab/services/ declaring it. This agent reads that directory,
 checks each declared entry against reality, and reports the result to
 homelab-api both periodically (a heartbeat, for the fleet-wide
 dashboard view -- see `homelab-cli fleet status`/`fleet drift`) and
 on demand (GET /status, authenticated the same "verify at every hop"
 way as every other internal request in this ecosystem, for
 up-to-the-second truth rather than as-of-the-last-heartbeat). A
 mismatch in either direction is the interesting signal: something
 declared but not running is a real outage; something running but
 undeclared is a surprise nothing else in this project would have
 caught. Replaces api.infrastructure_registry/`homelab-cli topology`.
 No database of its own -- every interaction with homelab-api is a
 plain HTTP call, authenticated as this host's own enrolled
 system_agent identity (see README.md's "Enrollment" section).
